  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c **** 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @brief Correlation of Q31 sequences.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length 2 * max(src
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * @details
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * The accumulator has a 2.62 format and maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplicatio
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * There is no saturation on intermediate additions.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * The input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * Scale down one of the inputs by 1/min(srcALen, srcBLen)to avoid overflows since a
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * maximum of min(srcALen, srcBLen) number of additions is carried internally.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * The 2.62 accumulator is right shifted by 31 bits and saturated to 1.31 format to yield the final
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * \par
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  * See <code>arm_correlate_fast_q31()</code> for a faster but less precise implementation of this f
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****  */
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c **** 
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c **** void arm_correlate_q31(
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****   q31_t * pSrcA,
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****   uint32_t srcALen,
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****   q31_t * pSrcB,
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****   uint32_t srcBLen,
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c ****   q31_t * pDst)
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q31.c **** {
